.TH HELIKODU 1 2026-11-18 Helikodu "User Commands"
.SH NAME
helikodu \- offline audio player and music library manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helikodu
.RB [ \-\-scheme
.IR scheme ]
.RB [ \-\-accent
.IR accent ]
.RB [ \-\-style
.IR style ]
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RI [ file \&...]
.br
.B helikodu
.B \-\-help
.br
.B helikodu
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B helikodu
is the desktop application of Helikodu, an audio player and music library
manager for Linux that works entirely offline.
It plays practically every audio format FFmpeg can decode, plays the sound
track of video files without showing any picture, and plays to the audio
device chosen in its settings, in shared or exclusive mode.
.PP
Files given on the command line are played.
Only one instance runs at a time: when Helikodu is already running, the files
are handed to it and the new process ends.
.PP
The output device, the library folders and every other setting are read from
the settings file; see
.BR FILES .
.SH OPTIONS
The appearance options override the settings for this start only.
.TP
.BI \-\-scheme " scheme"
The colour scheme:
.BR system ,
.B light
or
.BR dark .
.TP
.BI \-\-accent " accent"
The accent colour:
.B system
(the desktop's),
.BR amber ,
.BR blue ,
.B green
or
.BR violet .
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
The window style:
.B integrated
(the window draws its own title bar) or
.B classic
(the desktop's title bar, with an optional menu bar).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Shows invented sample content and plays nothing.
The library and the settings are not used.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Prints a short usage message and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the version and exits.
.PP
Options starting with
.B \-\-gapplication
are passed on to GApplication; desktop launchers use
.B \-\-gapplication\-service
to start Helikodu over D-Bus.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/helikodu/settings.toml
The settings
.RI ( ~/.config/helikodu/settings.toml
by default).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/helikodu/library.db
The library database: tracks, albums, ratings, play statistics and playlists
.RI ( ~/.local/share/helikodu/ ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/helikodu/
The last session
.RI ( session.json ),
the window state
.RI ( ui-state.toml )
and the marker of what is playing
.RI ( playing.json ),
which is used to recover after an abnormal end
.RI ( ~/.local/state/helikodu/ ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/helikodu/thumbnails/
Cover thumbnails; safe to delete
.RI ( ~/.cache/helikodu/ ).
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/helikodu/guide/index.html
The user guide, one page with every chapter and the FAQ.
.B F1
or
.B Help \[u203A] User Guide
opens it in the web browser; it is a local file, so it opens without a
network.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when an option is not recognised or the application cannot
start.
.SH EXAMPLES
Play two files:
.PP
.RS
.EX
helikodu ~/Music/one.flac ~/Music/two.opus
.EE
.RE
.PP
Look at the interface in light colours with sample content:
.PP
.RS
.EX
helikodu \-\-demo \-\-scheme light
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR helikodu\-cli (1),
.BR helikodu\-scan\-worker (1)
.PP
The user guide, installed with the application (see
.BR FILES )
and published at
.UR https://sorrelfox.github.io/helikodu/guide/
.UE .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/sorrelfox/helikodu/issues
.UE .
